---
layout: layout.njk
pagination:
  data: site.things
  size: 1
  alias: thing
permalink: '{{ thing.page }}'
eleventyComputed:
  title: '{{ thing.title }}'
  description: '{{ thing.summary }}'
  markdownTwin: '{{ thing.markdown }}'
---
{#- Links to another of Jamie's strip sites carry ?ref=xyz-<placement> (the ref filter, collection/sites.ts):
    "thing" for the thing itself (Where, the screenshot, the story's call to read it), "source" for the sources
    and the citations of connections and events. Feed, sitemap and evidence links are files, not visits, and
    the story text is content: both keep their links as written. #}
{#- Search (collection/search-index.ts): Pagefind indexes the article, which is the words of the thing: its
    title, summary, story, build, artifacts, connections and history. The crumbs, status line, pull quote, contents,
    record, screenshot, evidence, diagram and footer are left out. The empty image keeps Pagefind from taking the footer's photo as the page's
    image, whose address would match words like "avatars" on every page. #}
{#- The thing as an h-entry (IndieWeb): its title (p-name, without the sticker's letters), its canonical address
    (u-url), its author (p-author), its summary (p-summary) and its story (e-content). The author is the owner's
    h-card from data/sites.json, hidden, with the clean identity URL: the page already names Jamie in the footer
    (rel="me author"), and this says the entry is Jamie's too. It is the only microformat inside the entry, and
    Pagefind leaves it out. The entry has no dt-published: the dates a thing shows are when it started and ended,
    not when its page was published. #}
{#- Anchors: every section of the page and every artifact has an address of its own, so a link can point at
    one (/things/<id>/#artifacts, #artifact-<file>, #artifacts-<bundle>). The ids are fixed words and file names,
    never a heading's text, so a retitle never breaks a link someone sent. Each heading carries a small # link
    to its own address, the way to copy it; it is out of search and has a spoken name. #}
{% from "macros.njk" import shelf, permalink, artifactCard, picture %}
{#- The contents, as the rail beside the page and the fold above it on a phone. A count says how much is there. #}
{%- macro contents(thing) %}
{% if thing.body | trim %}<a class="toc-link" href="#story"><span>Story</span></a>
{% endif %}{% if thing.story and thing.story.engineering | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#build"><span>The build</span></a>
{% endif %}<a class="toc-link" href="#record"><span>The record</span></a>
{% if thing.artifacts | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#artifacts"><span>Artifacts</span><span class="toc-count">{{ thing.artifacts | length }}</span></a>
{% for bundle in thing.bundles %}<a class="toc-link toc-sub" href="#artifacts-{{ bundle.id }}"><span>{{ bundle.title }}</span><span class="toc-count">{{ bundle.artifacts | length }}</span></a>
{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if thing.activity %}<a class="toc-link" href="#activity"><span>Activity</span></a>
{% endif %}{% if thing.sources | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#sources"><span>Sources and evidence</span><span class="toc-count">{{ thing.sources | length }}</span></a>
{% endif %}{% if thing.connections | length or thing.inbound | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#connections"><span>Connections</span><span class="toc-count">{{ (thing.connections | length) + (thing.inbound | length) }}</span></a>
{% endif %}{% if thing.story and thing.story.related | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#related"><span>Related</span><span class="toc-count">{{ thing.story.related | length }}</span></a>
{% endif %}{% if thing.events | length %}<a class="toc-link" href="#history"><span>History</span><span class="toc-count">{{ thing.events | length }}</span></a>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro -%}
<article class="thing h-entry" data-pagefind-body>
  <span hidden data-pagefind-meta="image:"></span>
  <data class="u-url" value="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}"></data>
  <a class="p-author h-card" href="{{ owner.url }}" hidden data-pagefind-ignore>{{ owner.name }}</a>
  <header class="thing-header"{% if thing.story %} style="--accent: {{ thing.story.color }}"{% endif %}>
    <p class="crumbs" data-pagefind-ignore><a href="/things/">Things</a> · <a href="/things/#{{ thing.collection | slugify }}">{{ thing.collection }}</a></p>
    <h1 class="with-sticker">{% include "sticker.njk" %}<span class="p-name">{{ thing.title }}</span></h1>
    <p class="lede p-summary">{{ thing.summary }}</p>
    {% if thing.story %}<p class="introduction">{{ thing.story.introduction }}</p>{% endif %}
    <p class="thing-status-line" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <span class="status status-{{ thing.status }}">{{ thing.statusLabel }}</span>
      {%- if thing.started or thing.ended %}
      <span class="meta">
        {%- if thing.started %}Started <time datetime="{{ thing.started }}">{{ thing.started | date }}</time>{% endif %}
        {%- if thing.started and thing.ended %}. {% endif %}
        {%- if thing.ended %}Ended <time datetime="{{ thing.ended }}">{{ thing.ended | date }}</time>{% endif -%}
        {%- if thing.story and thing.story.started %} ({{ thing.story.started }}){% endif -%}
      </span>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if thing.url %}
      <a class="more" href="{{ thing.url | ref("thing") }}">{{ thing.url | replace("https://", "") }}</a>
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
  </header>

  {#- A line of Jamie's the page opens with (`pull` in the thing's front matter), from a question about this thing. #}
  {% if thing.pull %}
  <aside class="thing-words" aria-label="In his words" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <div>
      <p class="label">In his words</p>
      <p class="who"><span>Jamie, question {{ thing.pull.n }} · Session {{ thing.pull.session }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="pull">“<a href="{{ thing.pull.page }}">{{ thing.pull.words }}</a>”</blockquote>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  <details class="toc-fold" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <summary><span>On this page</span><span class="muted">Jump</span></summary>
    <nav aria-label="On this page">{{ contents(thing) }}</nav>
  </details>
  <div class="contents-grid">
  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page" data-toc data-pagefind-ignore>
    <p class="label">On this page</p>
    {{ contents(thing) }}
  </nav>
  <div class="thing-main">

  {% if thing.screenshot %}
  <figure class="screenshot" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <a href="{{ thing.screenshot.site | ref("thing") }}">{{ picture(thing.screenshot, thing.screenshot.alt, "(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px") }}</a>
    <figcaption>{{ thing.screenshot.place }} on {{ thing.screenshot.date | date }}. The collector grabs {{ thing.screenshot.page }} once a month.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.body | trim %}
  <section class="story e-content" id="story">
    {{ thing.body | md | safe }}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.story %}
  <section class="build" id="build">
    {% if thing.story.engineering | length %}
    <h2>The build {{ permalink("build", "The build") }}</h2>
    <ul>{% for item in thing.story.engineering %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if thing.story.stack | length %}
    <p class="stack">{% for item in thing.story.stack %}<span class="tag">{{ item }}</span> {% endfor %}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if thing.story.source %}
    <p><a href="{{ thing.story.source | ref("thing") }}">{{ thing.story.sourceLabel or "Source" }}</a></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- The rest of what the registry knows about the thing, and how it ties to the rest of the site. #}
  <section class="record" id="record" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2>The record {{ permalink("record", "The record") }}</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Status</dt>
      <dd><span class="status status-{{ thing.status }}">{{ thing.statusLabel }}</span> <span class="muted">{{ thing.statusDescription }}</span></dd>
      {% for row in site.timeline.rows %}{% if row.thing.id == thing.id %}
      <dt>Lifespan</dt>
      <dd class="thing-lifespan">{{ row | lifespan(site.timeline) | safe }} <span class="muted">Across the years from {{ site.timeline.firstYear }} to {{ site.timeline.lastYear }}. Each dot is an event in its history.</span></dd>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% if thing.stories | length %}
      <dt>{{ 'Story' if (thing.stories | length) == 1 else 'Stories' }}</dt>
      <dd class="thing-stories">{% for story in thing.stories %}<a href="{{ story.page }}">{{ story.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {%- if thing.interviews | length %}
      <dt>In his words</dt>
      <dd class="thing-interviews">{% for i in thing.interviews %}<a href="{{ i.page }}">{{ i.title }}</a>, {% for n in i.questions %}<a href="{{ i.page }}#q{{ n }}">question {{ n }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}{% if loop.revindex == 2 %} and {% else %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if thing.topicList | length %}
      <dt>Topics</dt>
      <dd>{% for topic in thing.topicList %}<a class="tag" href="{{ topic.page }}">{{ topic.title }}</a> {% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if thing.views %}
      <dt>Page views</dt>
      <dd class="views">{{ thing.views.total | number }} in the twelve months to {{ thing.views.until | date }} {{ thing.views.months | sparkline("Page views per month, counted by Tinylytics", "views") | safe }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if thing.latest %}
      <dt>Latest evidence</dt>
      <dd>{% if thing.latest.url %}<a href="{{ thing.latest.url }}">{{ thing.latest.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ thing.latest.label }}{% endif %}, {{ thing.latest.date | day }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
  </section>

  {#- Artifacts: a thing may put them in bundles, each a shelf that holds every piece of it, so an address like
      #artifact-<file> always lands on its piece. A large set also has a page of its own that shows them all at once
      (thing-artifacts.njk). #}
  {% if thing.artifacts | length %}
  <section class="artifacts" id="artifacts">
    <h2>Artifacts {{ permalink("artifacts", "Artifacts") }}</h2>
    <p class="muted">Files from the project itself, kept as they were.{% if thing.artifactsPage %} <a href="{{ thing.artifactsPage }}">All {{ thing.artifacts | length }} on one page</a>.{% endif %}</p>
    {% if thing.bundles | length %}
    {% for bundle in thing.bundles %}
    {% call shelf("artifacts-" + bundle.id, bundle.title, bundle.caption, bundle.cardWidth, (thing.artifactsPage + "#" + bundle.id) if (thing.artifactsPage and bundle.artifacts.length > 3), "All " + (bundle.artifacts | length), false, "h3", "artifact-bundle", true) %}
      {% for artifact in bundle.artifacts %}{{ artifactCard(artifact, "h4", "div", bundle.cardWidth) }}{% endfor %}
    {% endcall %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
    <ul class="artifact-list">
      {% for artifact in thing.artifacts %}{{ artifactCard(artifact, "h3") }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.activity %}
  {% set record = thing.activity %}
  <section class="thing-activity" id="activity" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2>Activity {{ permalink("activity", "Activity") }}</h2>
    {% if record.total %}<p>{{ { total: record.total, who: record.who } | activitySummary }}, {{ 'on' if record.total == 1 else 'the first on' }} {{ record.firstCommit | day }}.</p>{% endif %}
    {% if record.publications %}<p>{{ record.publications | number }} {{ 'publication' if record.publications == 1 else 'publications' }} collected from its feeds, the oldest from {{ record.firstPublication | day }}.</p>{% endif %}
    {% set columns = record | yearColumns(thing.title) %}
    {% if columns %}
    <figure class="year-chart">
      {{ columns | safe }}
      <figcaption>
        <span class="muted">Commits each year from {{ record.years[0].year }} to {{ (record.years | last).year }}{% if record.peak %}, most in {{ record.peak.year }} ({{ record.peak.total | number }}){% endif %}.</span>
        {% include "who-legend.njk" %}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% endif %}
    {% if record.recent | length %}
    <h3>The latest weeks with activity</h3>
    <ul class="activity-list">
      {% set weekHead = true %}
      {% for entry in record.recent %}{% include "activity-entry.njk" %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="muted"><a href="/years/">Year by year</a>, all of it. Who made each commit is from its author and co-author lines.</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.sources | length %}
  <section class="sources" id="sources" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <h2>Sources and evidence {{ permalink("sources", "Sources and evidence") }}</h2>
    <p class="muted">Checked every day from GitHub, sitemaps, feeds, the Internet Archive, and Tinylytics. Evidence never sets a status. That is Jamie’s call.</p>
    <ul class="source-list">
      {% for source in thing.sources %}
      <li class="source">
        {% if source.kind == 'github' %}
        <p class="source-head">
          <a href="https://github.com/{{ source.repository }}{% if source.path %}/tree/HEAD/{{ source.path }}{% endif %}">{{ source.repository }}{% if source.path %}/{{ source.path }}{% endif %}</a>
          <span class="role">{{ source.role }}</span>
          {% if source.observation and source.observation.archived %}<span class="role">archived on GitHub</span>{% endif %}
        </p>
        {% if source.observation %}
        {% set o = source.observation %}
        {% if o.description %}<p class="source-description">{{ o.description }}</p>{% endif %}
        <ul class="evidence">
          <li>Repository created {{ o.repositoryCreatedAt | day }} <span class="muted">(when the code started, not when it launched)</span></li>
          {% set reached = o | reach %}
          {% if reached %}<li>{{ reached }}</li>{% endif %}
          {% if o.languages | length %}<li>{{ o.languages | languages }}</li>{% endif %}
          {% if o.release %}<li>Latest release <a href="{{ o.release.url }}">{{ o.release.name }}</a>, {{ o.release.date | day }}</li>{% endif %}
          {% for scope in o.activity %}
          {% if (scope.path or none) == (source.path or none) %}
          <li>
            {% if scope.latestCommit %}Latest commit <a href="{{ scope.latestCommit.url }}">{{ scope.latestCommit.date | day }}</a>; {% endif %}
            {{ scope.count }}{% if not scope.complete %}+{% endif %} commits on {{ scope.branch }} between {{ scope.since | day }} and {{ scope.until | day }}
          </li>
          {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
          <li class="muted">Observed {{ o.observedAt | day }}</li>
        </ul>
        {% endif %}
        {% else %}
        <p class="source-head">
          <a href="{{ source.url | ref("source") }}">{{ source.url | replace("https://", "") }}</a>
          <span class="role">{{ source.role }}</span>
        </p>
        {% if source.observation or (source.captures and source.captures.firstCapture) or source.views %}
        {% set o = source.observation %}
        <ul class="evidence">
          {% if source.captures and source.captures.firstCapture %}
          <li>First archived <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/{{ source.captures.firstCapture | replace("-", "") }}/{{ source.captures.url }}">{{ source.captures.firstCapture | day }}</a> by the Internet Archive <span class="muted">(existence evidence, not a launch date)</span></li>
          {% endif %}
          {% if o and o.feed %}
          <li><a href="{{ o.feed.url }}">Feed</a>{% if o.feed.title %} “{{ o.feed.title }}”{% endif %}: {{ o.feed.items }} items{% if o.feed.newestPublished %}, newest {{ o.feed.newestPublished | day }}{% endif %}</li>
          {% endif %}
          {% if o and o.sitemap %}
          <li><a href="{{ o.sitemap.url }}">Sitemap</a>: {{ o.sitemap.pages | number }} pages{% if o.sitemap.newestModified %}, newest change {{ o.sitemap.newestModified | day }}{% endif %}</li>
          {% endif %}
          {% if source.views %}
          <li>{{ source.views.hits | number }} page views from {{ source.views.since | date }} to {{ source.views.until | date }}, counted by Tinylytics</li>
          {% endif %}
          <li class="muted">Observed {{ (o or source.captures or source.views).observedAt | day }}</li>
        </ul>
        {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="activity">
      {{ thing.months | sparkline("Commits and publications in the last twelve months") | safe }}
      <span class="muted">Commits and publications per month, last twelve months.</span>
    </p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.connections | length or thing.inbound | length %}
  <section class="connections" id="connections">
    <h2>Connections {{ permalink("connections", "Connections") }}</h2>
    {% set diagram = thing | connectionDiagram(site) %}
    {% if diagram %}
    <figure class="connection-diagram{% if not diagram.narrow %} wide-only{% endif %}" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <div class="diagram-wide">{{ diagram.wide | safe }}</div>
      {% if diagram.narrow %}<div class="diagram-narrow">{{ diagram.narrow | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
    </figure>
    {% endif %}
    <ul class="connection-list">
      {% for edge in thing.connections %}
      {% set other = site | thing(edge.to) %}
      <li{% if edge.kind == 'lineage' %} class="lineage"{% endif %}>
        <p><strong>{{ thing.title }}</strong> {{ edge.label }} <a href="{{ other.page }}">{{ other.title }}</a></p>
        <p class="muted">{{ edge.detail }} <a href="{{ edge.source | ref("source") }}">Source</a></p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for edge in thing.inbound %}
      {% set other = site | thing(edge.from) %}
      <li{% if edge.kind == 'lineage' %} class="lineage"{% endif %}>
        <p><a href="{{ other.page }}">{{ other.title }}</a> {{ edge.label }} <strong>{{ thing.title }}</strong></p>
        <p class="muted">{{ edge.detail }} <a href="{{ edge.source | ref("source") }}">Source</a></p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.story and thing.story.related | length %}
  <section class="related" id="related">
    <h2>Related {{ permalink("related", "Related") }}</h2>
    <p>{% for id in thing.story.related %}{% set other = site | thing(id) %}{% if other %}<a class="tag" href="{{ other.page }}">{{ other.title }}</a> {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if thing.events | length %}
  <section class="events" id="history">
    <h2>History {{ permalink("history", "History") }}</h2>
    <ol class="event-list">
      {% for event in thing.events %}
      <li>
        <time datetime="{{ event.date }}">{{ event.date | date }}</time>
        <span class="kind kind-{{ event.kind }}">{{ event.kind }}</span>
        <a href="{{ event | eventPage }}"><strong>{{ event.title }}</strong></a>
        <p>{{ event.summary }} <a href="{{ event.source | ref("source") }}">Source</a></p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <footer class="thing-footer" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <p class="muted">This thing as <a href="{{ thing.markdown }}">Markdown</a> · <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/content/things/{{ thing.id }}.md">Edit the record</a></p>
  </footer>
  </div>
  </div>
</article>
<script type="module" src="{{ assets.enhance }}"></script>
